+// line (a button beside it is fine) and the same start edge as the field above it. A text area, a check box or a
+// radio button between them ends the run, as does a field that starts elsewhere or stands right beside another
+// field on its line (at most 24 pixels between them); a field further off on the same line stands in another
+// column (the issue form's two columns), so each column is a run. A field that fills the box it stands in neither
+// sets nor takes the width. In a table in a form the fields alone in their cells of one column (the cells that
+// start at the same edge) are one run. Only min-width is set, never more than the box has room for; a run in a
+// part not shown yet (another tab, a collapsed fieldset) is measured once it shows.
